      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "aa6a9ee66486279a99aeafa3f7e015fc0ee751a470b1b6d4b688f1bd625ec6b0",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-5d356bbaac960a07",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, join an English-speaking group for a visit to the Arenal Hanging Bridges. The route leads through tropical forest, and the bridges offer views of the volcano.\n\nIn the afternoon, take a walk in Arenal Volcano National Park. The Los Tucanes Trail crosses the volcano’s southwestern slope and the hardened lava flows that reshaped the area during the 1968 eruption.\n\nOvernight at Arenal Kioro Suites & Spa. Meals: breakfast."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_alt:a85a5d89f0a7d06c",
      "field": "media.alt",
      "sourceTextSha256": "cc59430aa208a1f0de0fc0347784975d5031237f9f20610aab2c261fba636f6d",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-5d356bbaac960a07",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Palm trees and dense tropical forest near La Fortuna, Costa Rica"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_hover:82d057c51fe1e393",
      "field": "media.hover",
      "sourceTextSha256": "cd78b274c58e0a92f4807f8df0e1eb793352021860a80373adb73b36fdd7cbc6",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-5d356bbaac960a07",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "La Fortuna: a green, wooded valley and tall palms"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_title:f76823f601bc2496",
      "field": "itinerary.title",
      "sourceTextSha256": "8dc36808af2f4cd03e629d6f2ac3a92236bc68b38bd9ad18d45eb61ccf3e2c40",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-5d356bbaac960a07",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Arenal to the Tárcoles River and Manuel Antonio"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "865ff7515d1fad45610be3dd0d1d2c169bcff72659e777653497288e861ebd65",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-5d356bbaac960a07",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Travel with an English-speaking group to Puntarenas Province on the central Pacific coast.\n\nThe tour starts on the banks of the Río Grande de Tárcoles. Over the next 2 hours, you will take a boat trip down the Tárcoles River to its mouth and along the Guacalillo Canal. You may see American crocodiles up to 5 m long, sometimes close to the boat.\n\nUp to 50 bird species are found around the river, including macaws. After lunch, continue to Quepos, a tourist town near Manuel Antonio National Park.\n\nOvernight at Shana by the Beach Resort. Meals: breakfast and lunch."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_alt:5778e879c51120c3",
      "field": "media.alt",
      "sourceTextSha256": "4aff6c1d58f2d477d26a6967dd27a662152614148a7afcf954e4e94bfdd0b498",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-5d356bbaac960a07",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Boats on the lake below Arenal Volcano, Costa Rica"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_hover:0ff49a543cadd6a5",
      "field": "media.hover",
